module gunbc.repository

import std.types { String, Bool, NonEmptyStr, Int }
import extdeps.github.github { Repository }

data gunbc_repository_authority_note: String = "ONE TYPED ROW FOR THE REPOSITORY THIS PROJECT LIVES IN, because before it there were five spellings and no authority. dag/gunbc/instruments/ci_heal_dispatch carried owner and repo as two bare Strings, dag/gunbc/tools/review and review_codex each carried their own owner/repo pair, dag/gunbc/runner_host_deploy carried org, and dag/gunbc/assimilate/bmc_token_federation carried the slug gunb-ai/gunbc as a third shape again. Five nicknames for one entity is the DESIGN section 3 violation exactly, and it is the kind that stays invisible because every individual literal looks obviously correct.\\n\\nWHY A SIXTH SPELLING WOULD NOT HAVE BEEN ACCEPTABLE, which is the reviewer's point (review 46301) and is correct: an honestly-marked scaffold duplicating a canonical fact is still a violation - DESIGN says so in as many words in its recurring-failure list. The answer to five nicknames is not a sixth carrying a promise to consolidate later; it is one authority the others CONSUME. So this row exists and the five sites now project from it.\\n\\nWHY THE TYPE IS Repository RATHER THAN A PAIR OF STRINGS. extdeps.github.github models what the GitHub API actually returns, so owner, name, full_name, private and default_branch travel together as one fact with one identity. A consumer that needs the default branch stops guessing main, and a consumer that needs the slug stops concatenating one. The bare-String sites could only ever answer the question they were spelled for.\\n\\nWHY IT LIVES IN gunbc RATHER THAN extdeps. The TYPE is an upstream fact and belongs to extdeps; WHICH repository this project is, is a product fact about this project. Putting the instance in extdeps would make the dependency model know about its dependent."

data gunbc_repository: Repository = Repository {
  owner: "gunb-ai",
  name: "gunbc",
  full_name: "gunb-ai/gunbc",
  private: false,
  default_branch: "main",
}

// THE NUMERIC IDENTITY OF THIS REPOSITORY, READ FROM THE FORGE (repos/gunb-ai/gunbc, 2026-09-17:
// id 1143718943, owner.id 244123794). It is a SECOND fact about the same repository, not a second
// spelling of the first: a name can be released, re-registered by someone else, or transferred, and
// an id cannot, which is why Google's workload-identity guidance for GitHub tells a trust condition
// to pin `repository_id` and `repository_owner_id` rather than the names. The one consumer today is
// gunbc.auth.heal_publisher_federation's attribute condition, where a name would make the trust
// boundary cybersquattable.
type RepositoryNumericIdentity {
  repository_id: Int
  owner_id: Int
}

data gunbc_repository_numeric_identity: RepositoryNumericIdentity = RepositoryNumericIdentity {
  repository_id: 1143718943,
  owner_id: 244123794,
}

// THE SECOND REPOSITORY THIS PROJECT COMPOSES WITH, and it lives here for the reason the note above
// gives for the first: WHICH repositories this project is are product facts, and one authority the
// others consume beats a spelling per consumer. gunbc.workspace_repository_materialisation reads
// this row to say which prefixes hold material that must never be tracked in the public tree, and
// gunbc.gitignore_emit derives the ignore rows from its visibility -- so a flip at the forge is a
// change to THIS row and the projection follows.
//
// Every field is OBSERVED from the GitHub repository object rather than assumed, read 2026-09-14
// via the repos/gunb-ai/gunbc-private endpoint: full_name, private and default_branch came back
// gunb-ai/gunbc-private, true and main. default_branch in particular is not inferred from the
// public repository's -- a sibling repository is free to differ, and a guessed field is exactly the
// kind of quietly-wrong fact that survives until something acts on it.
data gunbc_private_repository: Repository = Repository {
  owner: "gunb-ai",
  name: "gunbc-private",
  full_name: "gunb-ai/gunbc-private",
  private: true,
  default_branch: "main",
}
